<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59937" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρίβᾰν-ος</span></b> , ὁ, 
			Att.
		 for <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλίβανος</span></b>  (which
		is called 
			Dor.
		 in <i><span class="en">
			<u>EM</u>
			538.19
		</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
			Epich.
			143
		</span></i>, and is the usu. form in Pap., <i><span class="en">
			<u>PPetr.</u>
			3p.328
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, etc.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>covered earthen vessel</i>, wider at bottom than at top,
			wherein bread was baked by putting hot embers round it, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.92
			</span></i> (in form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλιβ</span>-), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				309
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>V.</u>
				1153
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				176.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτως εἰμὶ ὡς εἰς κρίβανον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					1842.7
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(vi A. D.)</span>; <i>potter's oven,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PCair.Zen.
				271.9
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλ</span>-).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>funnel-shaped vessel</i>, used for drawing water, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				16.2.13
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλ</span>-). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>underground channel</i> or <i>vaulted passage</i>, in
			irrigation works, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				7188.17
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλ</span>-).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hollow, cavern in a rock</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				2.22
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
